hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3039","Narrated to us Hārūn ibn Isḥāq, narrated to us ʿAbdah ibn Sulaymān, on the authority of Saʿīd, on the authority of Qatādah, on the authority of ʿAzrah, on the authority of Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās (RA) that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) heard a man saying: *\"Labbayka ʿan Shubrumah\"* (Here I am for Shubrumah).\n\nSo he (ﷺ) asked: *\"Who is Shubrumah?\"*\n\nThe man replied: *\"My brother or a close relative of mine.\"*\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) then asked: *\"Have you performed Hajj yourself?\"*\n\nThe man said: *\"No.\"*\n\nSo the Prophet (ﷺ) said: *\"Then make this Hajj for yourself, and then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.\"*\n\n**Commentary:**\nAbū Bakr (RA) said: *\"In this narration, it is clarified that if a person has not performed Hajj for himself, it is not permissible for him to perform Hajj on behalf of another, even if the latter is deceased.\"*\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
